From 5ba30e6dd8bd042cd9f6229f9cfcf99409565f0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeltaTor <deltator@example.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:23:17 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 36/38] conflux: add a quiet ConfluxProbeLog level and stop the
 startup leak

ConfluxProbeLog gained a third, quiet level, and two defects found while
analysing a real Windows probe log are fixed.

Level 3 keeps level 2's suppression of tor's own log lines but replaces the
per-event mechanism lines (window opens, rolls, candidate tables, picks) with
a single summary line per minute: window/roll/trusted/decayed counters, the
number of picks, the fastest candidate, the floor, the total weight, how many
candidates are still at zero and the set chosen last. Like the rest of the
probe it is emitted lazily when a stream is placed, so an idle client writes
nothing. This makes the diagnostics usable for long runs: level 2 produced
roughly 6.7 MB per 1000 picks in the captured log.

The 16 startup lines that still appeared at the top of a level-2 log were the
messages tor buffers before the Log targets exist and then replays once they
do. The replay in flush_log_messages_from_startup() bypasses logv(), so it did
not see the filter; apply the same filter there. Levels 2 and 3 log files now
start directly with mechanism output.

The log filter is now a level instead of a boolean, so
log_set_conflux_mthr_only() becomes log_set_conflux_mthr_level() and the
config code passes the option through unchanged (validated as 0-3).
